WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 line:92%
-First of all, congratulations.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
This film is so fantastic.
-Thank you so much!

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:05.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You co-wrote it, you starred
in it, you directed it.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have directed things
before.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've never directed horror
before, though?

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-And --

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why would I do that?
-Yeah, I mean --

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
It didn't seem like a fit
for me either.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's the number-one movie
in the country.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did it come about?
How did this --

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.086 line:92%
-It was really interesting.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.389
I was about to start this show
"Jack Ryan" that I was doing,

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.758
and some of the producers
had this script, and they said,

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Would you ever act
in a horror movie?"

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.029
And I said, "Ooh, I don't do
horror, but thanks anyway."

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said,
"It's about a family that

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.098
can't make any noise,
and you have to figure out why."

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.568
And I went, "Damn it!" That's
one of the best one-liners ever.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.805 size:84% position:42%
And I read this script,
and legitimately, yes,

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love that everybody says
it's scary, and it is.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really great, but there
was something in there,

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
the deeper theme there
is parenthood.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:49.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I actually was holding
our 3-week-old daughter

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
while reading this script
about a family

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.053 size:81% position:41%
that would do anything
to protect their kids,

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like, "Oh, my God."
-Yeah.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:58.291 size:78% position:39%
-I was using the baby
to wipe the tears.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.127
Which, by the way, we have
to talk about your baby!

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.529 size:78% position:39%
-Well, I -- you know,
I do want to say --

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.499 line:92%
-Thank you, guys. Thank you.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And don't worry,
I'll bring it full circle

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:09.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
back to the movie.
I'm selfish.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.271
-Yeah, no, I want to tie it in.
-I want to talk about

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
this lobby hero you became.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, look, I --
my wife was the hero,

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.243 size:84% position:42%
but I -- it does tie in
to the movie because

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would have thought
the most terrifying birth

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
this weekend was --
there's a birth in this movie.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, this is a movie

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
about you have to be quiet
or else the monsters.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.655
-Yeah.
-And so Emily has to do a scene

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.690 size:84% position:42%
where she's birthing
without making a noise.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's terrifying.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's terrifying.
-And then your wife,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.795
your actual wife gives birth
in the lobby, and you're like,

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"That was nothing."

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you think
monsters are scary,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
but nothing's more scary
than like,

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.902 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Oh, my God, our doorman

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
is going to see
my wife's genitals."

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, so --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
So wait, I just --
I thought about that doorman

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.944
when you were telling the story.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you sort of
skipped past him.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You were like,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.515
"There's a doorman --" and then
you thanked him very nicely.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I just imagined
what that guy's doing, like,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, Seth, how you doing?"
"You guys go" --

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my God, it's a baby.
Oh, it's a baby.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a baby
in your sweat pants!"

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, did you shut him down
forever?

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.395 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I got to be honest.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I hope he doesn't
take this the wrong way --

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.500 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I wasn't focused on him.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, during the birth...
-It's fine.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...I was like,
"I hope Kevin's okay."

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, but it was --
they were great

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I only know
they were great, like,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
after the fact because
they did, like,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.813
kind of corral the people
in our building to be like,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You can't go in the lobby
right now."

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:30.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they were like,
"There's wet here. It's wet.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Guys, it's wet.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just careful, careful."
-But it's like --

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.954 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's a beautiful wet.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:35.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
But yeah, so --
-Oh, that's my band name.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was -- it was --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My new band name.
-Oh, but you know --

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
you mentioned you had
a 3-week-old.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got a 4-year-old
and a 2-year-old.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Almost 2.
-Almost 2.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we got a two-year gap
with ours, as well.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is --
how is the second one --

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.405 line:92%
how did it change the game?

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:53.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In every single way.
-Yeah.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.910
-Because the --
when you have your first child,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.712 size:75% position:38%
it's amazing, but in
those moments where

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
